.TH MDTREE 1 "August 2026" "mdtree 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdtree \- Markdown Tree Visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdtree
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR | \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdtree
is a highly customizable command-line utility that reads Markdown files and outputs their structural representation, similar to how the `tree` command visualizes directory structures.
.PP
It provides an elegant, color-coded way to quickly review document hierarchies, view headings, content, lists, blockquotes, and tables without opening the file in an editor. Supports Markdown syntax including headings, unordered/ordered lists, task lists, blockquotes, fenced code blocks, tables, and horizontal rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-depth " \fI<level>\fR"
Limit the display to a certain heading level (1-6). A value of 7 shows all content.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-find " \fI<string>\fR"
Search the file for the given string (case-sensitive) and show matched lines.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-case-insensitive
Make the search case-insensitive when used with \-f or \-r.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-regex " \fI<regex>\fR"
Search the file using a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-ignore " \fI<regex>\fR"
Ignore headings (and their children) matching the regex.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-headings-only
Strictly show only headings (like a Table of Contents).
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-focus " \fI<regex>\fR"
Focus on the first heading matching the regex and only show its subtree.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-no-pager
Disable automatic `less` paging.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-no-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ascii
Use ASCII characters for tree branches instead of box-drawing characters.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stats
Print statistics about the parsed files at the end.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-line-numbers
Show original line numbers next to each tree item.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-no-warnings
Suppress linter warnings at the end of the output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show a table of contents (headings only):
.RS
mdtree -H README.md
.RE
.PP
Focus on a specific API Endpoint section in a large document:
.RS
mdtree -F "API Endpoints" docs.md
.RE
.PP
Find occurrences of a specific word or phrase:
.RS
mdtree -f "installation" manual.md
.RE
.PP
Combine flags for advanced filtering:
.RS
mdtree -F "Installation" -d 3 README.md
.RE
.SH BUGS
See the issue tracker on GitHub for open bugs or feature requests.
